    "perplexity": {
      "description": "It Means Everything is Save Ferris’s debut full-length album, originally released in 1997 and now returning on its first-ever vinyl pressing through the 2026 Parting Gift Records reissue. The record captures the band at the peak of the third-wave ska era, mixing brisk horn-driven energy, sharp pop hooks, and a Southern California punk edge that helped define their sound.\n\nThe album’s best-known track, “Come on Eileen,” became Save Ferris’s breakthrough hit, but the set also showcases the band’s knack for catchy, upbeat songwriting across originals like “The World Is New,” “Superspy,” and “Goodbye.” In its original form, It Means Everything was a lively, radio-ready ska-pop statement; the 2026 vinyl edition gives that era-defining debut a long-awaited physical format that should appeal to collectors and fans of 1990s alternative rock.",
